Hello,
I am trying to undertake distance sampling for marine mammals found within offshore oil fields in Ghana, particularly during oil field development projects. The purpose is to help predict the likelihood of these animals being impacted upon by the anthropogenic stress associated with the operations. the area is noted for pilot whales and bottlenose dolphins.
The marine platform to be used as an observation platform is DP pipelay vessel which may keep single positions for longer hours during the operation with limited manoeuvring at very slow speed. Since line transect is most used for marine mammal surveys, how can I incorporate this into a study of a specific area on a platform restricted in manoeuvrability?
Is it, therefore, advisable to implement point transect survey in examining the area since it most likely reflects the nature of the operation.

Regards to everyone

